      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The TPS program allows foreign nationals of a country designated by the Government as having unusually bad or dangerous conditions to live and work in the United States while the conditions last."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "722302f40908396c270408f2d7191953217f292f724dbd52bd645719192d0cc0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-722302f40908-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari, 592 U. S. \u2013\u2013\u2013 (2021), to resolve a Circuit split over whether a TPS recipient who entered the country unlawfully can still become an LPR."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "722302f40908396c270408f2d7191953217f292f724dbd52bd645719192d0cc0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-722302f40908-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sanchez resists this conclusion by asserting an \u201cindissoluble relationship between admission and nonimmigrant status.\u201d Reply Brief 2 (emphasis in original). While conceding that some forms of status (e. g., asylum) do not require admission, Sanchez contends that nonimmigrant status always does: \u201cOne cannot obtain lawful nonimmigrant status without admission.\u201d Ibid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-315",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "722302f40908396c270408f2d7191953217f292f724dbd52bd645719192d0cc0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-722302f40908-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He therefore cannot become a permanent resident of this country."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
